    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0505" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4682: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-16T10:00:00+02:00">July 16, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>382. My 366, July 10, 8 p.m. I have learned that the new Russsian Minister here
                    has now assured the German Minister<anchor n="71" xml:id="d517-f1"/> that Russia
                    will not go further in Rumania. For what it is worth and insofar as he may be
                    informed of his Government’s real intentions from day to day this is noteworthy
                    in that the declaration was made to the German Minister and by him communicated
                    to his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d517-f1" n="71" xml:id="d517-f1-content">
                <p>Wilhelm Fabricius.</p>
